# Add exact per-repository exceptions here for trusted upstream URLs that are
# known to fail automated validation. Keep entries narrow and documented.
#
# Example:
# https://cmsweb.cern.ch/das/

# docs.gitlab.com serves lychee a 403 and bounces the request through a
# GitLab OAuth sign-in redirect; the same URLs open fine in a browser.
https://docs.gitlab.com/ee/ci/pipelines/job_artifacts.html
https://docs.gitlab.com/ee/ci/yaml/README.html#special-yaml-features

# docs.gitlab.com has reorganised these pages, so the anchors no longer
# resolve even though the pages themselves redirect successfully.
https://docs.gitlab.com/ee/administration/instance_limits.html#number-of-jobs-in-active-pipelines
https://docs.gitlab.com/ee/ci/yaml/#configuration-parameters

# Dead personal project on CERN GitLab, kept as the worked example that
# illustrates the `<project-url>/-/ci/lint` pattern in 06-hello-world-ci.
https://gitlab.cern.ch/gfidalgo/ci-testing/-/ci/lint
